    "body": "- [ X] I have searched open and closed issues for duplicates\r\nIt's a resurgence of #3235 and #2202 with the latest version iOS and MacOS clients.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n### Bug Description\r\n\r\nI left a group on mobile and it behaves appropriately (cannot send or receive messages, disappearing messages expire on time). But when I use the desktop client, the group is not only present, but I can still send and receive messages.\r\n\r\n### Steps to Reproduce\r\n1. Leave group on mobile device (iOS, iPhone 11). \r\n2. Open desktop client, click on group.\r\n\r\nActual Result:\r\n1. See latest messages (recent, prior to disappearing) in desktop client.\r\n2. Send messages to group that I left. \r\n\r\nExpected Result:\r\n- To not be able to see any new messages from the group I departed.\r\n- To not be able to send any messages from the group I departed.\r\n\r\n### Screenshots\r\n\r\nExcluded for privacy.\r\n\r\n### Platform Info\r\n\r\nSignal Version:\r\n\r\nDesktop: v1.34.2\r\nMobile: 3.10.5.3\r\n\r\n\r\nOperating System:\r\n\r\nmacOS Catalina 10.15.5\r\n\r\nLinked Device Version:\r\n\r\niOS 13.5\r\n\r\n### Link to Debug Log\r\nhttps://debuglogs.org/63939213a1002d3bf846836bbdae5995d76d13ced2c399a3d5ceedd6114664c9\r\n",
